######MDVR Temperature Alarm Configuration
```xml
&lt;VariCfgSec Action=&quot;DEVICE_SET&quot;&gt;&lt;stTempAlarm&gt;&lt;stTempAlarmPara&gt;&lt;Temp_0 ucFD_TempType=&quot;0&quot; ucFD_LowTempEnable=&quot;1&quot; fFD_LowTemp=&quot;30&quot; ucFD_HighTempEnable=&quot;1&quot; fFD_HighTemp=&quot;35&quot; /&gt;&lt;/stTempAlarmPara&gt;&lt;/stTempAlarm&gt;&lt;/VariCfgSec&gt;
```
&gt; Parameter Notes:
ucFD_LowTempEnable=”1” Low-temperature enable: 1 = On, 0 = Off
fFD_LowTemp=”25” Low-temperature threshold: 25°
ucFD_HighTempEnable=”1” High-temperature enable: 1 = On, 0 = Off
fFD_HighTemp=”30.000000” High-temperature threshold: 30°
Rule Description: Set the high-temperature alarm to 10°C. An alarm triggers once when the temperature reaches 10°, and triggers again when the temperature rises by 0.5°, continuing in this manner. The same applies to the low-temperature alarm. The “Alarm Start Time” is the time the alarm is triggered, and the “Alarm End Time” is the time the alarm is cleared. The alarm ends when the temperature remains below 10° for the specified duration.
